<!-- Batch D1 violations 2.1 fixture: each 2.1-applicable batch-D1 rule fires
     exactly once. One dedicated violator per rule; everything else compliant so
     nothing fires twice:
       IG.AE ItemRefs: 71 (dup KeySequence on IT.USUBJID ref), 72 (KeySequence
         "A"), 66 (OrderNumber "1.5"), 68 (Mandatory "Maybe"), 69 (no Mandatory),
         75 (IsNonStandard "No"), 77 (HasNoData "No"), 79 (def:WhereClauseRef),
         73 (no MethodOID on Derived IT.AEDUR), 74 (dangling MT.MISSING),
         242 (HasNoData Yes but IT.AEHND has no CommentOID), 147 (IT.AENOSAS has
         no SASFieldName), 168 (IT.AENODESC has no Description), 154+155
         (IT.AENOORIG has neither Origin nor ValueListRef)
       IG.KS: 70 (no KeySequence anywhere; no OrderNumbers so 238 stays silent)
       IG.ON: 238 (mixed OrderNumber: one with, one without)
       VL.LB / IT.LB.PH / IT.LBORRES: 142 (value Length 200 > variable Length 20)
       Unreferenced ItemDefs (each with an otherwise-valid Origin so 154 stays
         at one finding): 137 (no OID), 138 (no Name), 139 (no DataType),
         140 (DataType "string"), 141 (text without Length), 143 (date with
         Length), 144 (Length "0"), 145 (float without SignificantDigits),
         146 (SignificantDigits "-1"), 148 (dangling COM.MISSING), 169 (two
         Descriptions), 158 (Origin without Type), 159 (Collected/Subject
         without DocumentRef), 159-B (DocumentRef leafID not the aCRF),
         160 (Type "Recorded"), 161 (Source "CRO"), 243 (Origin with two
         Descriptions)
     DEFINE-XML-0160-B is 2.0-only and version-gated here. -->
